From 4deddb43227087105f26473fd3e577c43e87d83a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vortiago <atle@havso.net>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 13:40:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] perf(ggml-cpu): split wide rows across threads in get_rows
 and dup_bytes
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A recurrent model loads the state of each layer with a get_rows of one
row per sequence. For Qwen3-Next style models that row is 3 MiB. In a
model graph every node gets all threads, but get_rows_f32 split the
work by rows, so only min(nr, nth) threads, one or two, copied the
state. The state snapshot cpy into a strided cache view took the
copy-by-rows branch of dup_bytes, which split the work by ne01 =
n_seqs, so again one or two threads copied every snapshot.

- get_rows_f32: with fewer F32 or I32 rows than threads and rows of at
  least 4096 elements, each thread copies one cache-line-sized range
  of every row. This also covers the narrower conv state rows.
- dup_bytes: the copy-by-rows branch moves to its own function and
  splits all ne01*ne02*ne03 rows. With fewer rows than threads, each
  thread copies one cache-line-sized range of every row.
- ggml_get_n_tasks: a graph in which every node has n_tasks = 1 runs
  on one thread, so the column split had no threads to use there. Such
  graphs are a single-op test-backend-ops graph, or a CPU split that
  holds only the state get_rows under GPU offloading. A get_rows of
  fewer F32 or I32 rows than threads, with rows of at least 65536
  elements, now asks for all threads. That width is above any token
  embedding row, so the get_rows of embeddings with GPU offloading
  keeps n_tasks = 1 (see the FIXME). In a model graph with mul_mats
  this changes nothing.

Both are plain copies, so the output is bit-exact. Both splits are off
under use_ref, which keeps a row split (over all rows for dup_bytes),
so test-backend-ops compares the new splits with a row split. New
GET_ROWS and CPY cases cover a 3 MiB row, a row width that is not a
multiple of a cache line, and a strided Q8_0 copy. The GET_ROWS cases
with one row reach the column split from 2 test threads, and the CPY
cases with two rows from 3.

Design I4 part A (arbiter perf plan), from a reading of ops.cpp.

